Data tables taken from specifications:

internal/entity/entities.txt
  The named character references of the WHATWG HTML Living Standard,
  section 13.5 "Named character references", whose machine-readable form
  is https://html.spec.whatwg.org/entities.json. The HTML Standard is
  (c) WHATWG (Apple, Google, Mozilla, Microsoft) and licensed under the
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License.
  The file in this repository was written from the content of that list
  without network access; internal/entity/gen.go regenerates it from
  entities.json, and the result should be compared with it.

internal/charset/charset.go (win1252High) and the encoding labels
  From the WHATWG Encoding Standard (index-windows-1252 and the table of
  encoding labels), (c) WHATWG, CC BY 4.0.

internal/charset/tables.go, dbcs.go, cp932.txt, cp936.txt, cp949.txt,
cp950.txt, gen/gen_dbcs.py
  Copied from go-fast-rtf (internal/codepage, commit b756076), same
  author and licence. There:
  - tables.go holds the upper halves of the single-byte code pages, the
    content of the Unicode Consortium's mapping files MAPPINGS/VENDORS/
    MICSFT/WINDOWS/CP874.TXT and CP1250.TXT to CP1258.TXT, and MAPPINGS/
    VENDORS/APPLE/ROMAN.TXT, compared byte by byte with Python's codecs
    of the same code pages with no difference.
  - cp932.txt to cp950.txt were generated by gen/gen_dbcs.py from
    Python's codecs cp932, cp936, cp949 and cp950, which implement
    Microsoft's code pages as the Unicode Consortium publishes them
    (MAPPINGS/VENDORS/MICSFT/WINDOWS/CP932.TXT ... CP950.TXT). Mappings to
    C1 controls and the Private Use Area that the codecs add beyond the
    published files are left out. The first line of each names the
    Python version.
  The mapping data is used under the Unicode terms of use.

internal/css/color.go (namedColors)
  The named colors of the W3C CSS Color Module Level 4, section 6.1.
